|~ qlang operand catalog — axis family. Reflective navigation
   from a value to the declaration it names. A Keyword `:foo`
   names the binding its scope holds under the name, one the
   query, the session or a module's `use` wrote, and a verb of a
   provider is read by its address, `::vec/filter`; a TagKeyword
   `::Foo` names the tag's declaration; every other value names
   the declaration of its kind, the kind `type` answers, so
   `5 | docs` reads the page of `::number` and a value tagged
   `::Box` reads the page of `::Box`, and the record `env` answers
   reads the binding it records. Each axis projects the record
   the declaration wrote into its scope, `::binding`, whose step
   is a `BindStep` — `source` the
   declaration as a Quote, `docs` the attached doc-prefix Vec of
   Doc-values, `examples` every `~(…)` Quote segment from those
   docs ready for `runExamples` to fire. ~|

:source
  |~~ `:name | source` — Quote of the `BindStep` that binds `:name`
      in its scope, the `:source` of its record, which `parse`
      prints as its text; `::Tag | source` the tag's. A binding no
      step declared, a value `use` or a host bound, answers null.
      Any other value reads the declaration of its kind.

      ~(::vec/filter | source | parse | contains ":filter")
      ~(::AddLeftNotNumberError | source | parse | contains "AddLeftNotNumberError")
      ~("text" | source | eq (::string | source))
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/source
            :category :axis
            :subject :any
            :returns [:quote :null]}

::SourceBindingNotFoundError
  |~~ `source` — no declaration found for the name it read: a
      keyword that names no binding of its scope, the name of a
      verb a provider keeps among them, or a tag name that names
      nothing. `:addresses` holds the addresses where the verbs of
      that name live.

      ~(
        :nonexistent-binding | source
        !| [type /bindingName]
        |  eq [::SourceBindingNotFoundError :nonexistent-binding]
       )
      ~(:filter | source !| /addresses | has ::vec/filter)
  ~~|

:docs
  |~~ `:name | docs` — Vec of Doc-values, one per attached doc-prefix
      on the `BindStep` that binds `:name` in its scope, and
      `::vec/filter | docs` the page of a verb by its address. Each
      Doc-value `/segments`
      surfaces TaggedLit and Quote inline structure for navigation;
      Quote segments are the evaluable examples `runExamples` runs.
      Any other value reads the page of its kind, and the `:kind`
      field of a map names nothing: the map reads the page of
      `::map`.

      ~(::vec/filter | docs | first | /content | contains "predicate")
      ~(::AddLeftNotNumberError | docs | first | type | eq ::doc)
      ~(5 | docs | eq (::number | docs))
      ~({:kind ::set} | docs | eq (::map | docs))
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/docs
            :category :axis
            :subject :any
            :returns :vec}

::DocsBindingNotFoundError
  |~~ `docs` — no declaration found for the name it read: a
      keyword that names no binding of its scope, the name of a
      verb a provider keeps among them, or a tag name that names
      nothing. `:addresses` holds the addresses where the verbs of
      that name live.

      ~(
        :nonexistent-binding | docs
        !| [type /bindingName]
        |  eq [::DocsBindingNotFoundError :nonexistent-binding]
       )
      ~(:filter | docs !| /addresses | has ::vec/filter)
  ~~|

:examples
  |~~ `:name | examples` — Vec of Quote-values extracted from the
      binding's docs. `runExamples` consumes this Vec to evaluate
      each Quote against an isolated env; `:ok` is true iff the
      example answers true. Any other value reads the examples of
      its kind.

      ~(::vec/filter | examples | count | gt 0)
      ~(::vec/filter | examples | first | parse | contains "filter")
      ~(5 | examples | eq (::number | examples))
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/examples
            :category :axis
            :subject :any
            :returns :vec}

::ExamplesBindingNotFoundError
  |~~ `examples` — no declaration found for the name it read: a
      keyword that names no binding of its scope, the name of a
      verb a provider keeps among them, or a tag name that names
      nothing. `:addresses` holds the addresses where the verbs of
      that name live.

      ~(
        :nonexistent-binding | examples
        !| [type /bindingName]
        |  eq [::ExamplesBindingNotFoundError :nonexistent-binding]
       )
      ~(:filter | examples !| /addresses | has ::vec/filter)
  ~~|

:spec
  |~~ `:name | spec` — env-side declaration descriptor Map for the
      named binding. Operand declarations surface as
      `{:impl :qlang/prim/<name> :category … :subject …
      :modifiers … :returns … :throws … :captured … :effectful …}`
      with identity `::builtin` on the JS-header slot (reachable
      through `:name | spec | type`). `:captured` and `:effectful`
      are stamped from the resolved primitive at bootstrap, and
      `:throws` is read back off the sites that record this binding
      as their `:operand`; the rest is authored in the catalog
      body. Error tags surface as
      `{:category :typeError :operand … :position … :expectedType
      …}`, every field of it stamped at bootstrap from the throw
      site that records it — the catalog side of an error tag
      carries the prose and the example segments `docs` and
      `examples` answer with. The constructors of kinds surface as
      `{:impl :qlang/type/<tag> :throws […]}`. All three carry the
      same `::builtin` header identity.
      A declared verb surfaces as its signature, a `::spec~(…)`;
      any other binding as the value its record holds. Any other
      value reads the descriptor of its kind. A built-in declared as a
      verb on its noun surfaces as its signature too, its noun the
      subject and its refusals `:throws`, and a projection of a
      signature reads the body of the declaration it names [D72].

      The discriminator path for per-tag static facts attached
      to any tagged value — `result !| spec | /category`
      reads `:typeError` off the error tag the error carries;
      `::number/add | spec | /throws` lists the per-site error
      classes `add` raises, and each of those names `:add` back on
      its own `/operand`.

      ~(::number/add | spec | /subject | eq ::number)
      ~(::AddLeftNotNumberError | spec | /operand | eq :add)
      ~(::verb | spec | /impl | eq :qlang/type/verb)
      ~(:twice ::verb~(:x ::number | mul 2) | :twice | spec | type | eq ::spec)
      ~("x" | add 1 !| spec | /category | eq :typeError)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/spec
            :category :axis
            :subject :any
            :returns :map}

::SpecBindingNotFoundError
  |~~ `spec` — no declaration found for the name it read: a
      keyword that names no binding of its scope, the name of a
      verb a provider keeps among them, or a tag name that names
      nothing. `:addresses` holds the addresses where the verbs of
      that name live.

      ~(
        :nonexistent-binding | spec
        !| [type /bindingName]
        |  eq [::SpecBindingNotFoundError :nonexistent-binding]
       )
      ~(:filter | spec !| /addresses | has ::vec/filter)
  ~~|
